{
 "id": 76491,
 "name": "Internet Protocol Identity Community Group",
 "is_closed": true,
 "creation-date": "2015-02-15",
 "description": "This group is for the discussion of assigning an IPv6 address for every person on Earth, so everyone has a digital identity.\r\n\r\nEach individual could use this to proxy or alias other identifiers, permanent or temporary, over different spans of their lifetime. Thus, a person they can manage their domain names, physical or email addresses, phone numbers, WebRTC address, and other contact info as they wish, flexibly maintaining an identity in a decentralized way not controlled by third-party commercial interests or even governments.\r\n\r\nThis system could also be used for organizations, businesses, animals, or any other entity that needs an identity.\r\n\r\nThis group may produce specifications.",
